    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            145,
            412
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The print theme names one family for everything, so the sans stack and the\nmonospace stack are the only two a document can reach without embedding a font\nof its own. Four faces come out of the first stack and the styles applied to\nit, and the code font is the second."
        }
      ],
      "position": [
        145,
        412
      ],
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "position": [
            414,
            436
          ],
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Body text is regular. "
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "position": [
                438,
                485
              ],
              "type": "text",
              "value": "Bold is a different face, not a heavier stroke."
            }
          ],
          "position": [
            436,
            487
          ],
          "type": "strong"
        },
        {
          "position": [
            487,
            488
          ],
